# C10.1-C10.4: `use` works under both backends, including below the top level,
# and a method call on a Java value that arrived from a compiled call still
# reaches Java.
#
# The nested `use` is the part that used to be refused: ADR-0064 made it a
# compile error and ADR-0066 replaced that with a run-time registration into
# `dev.oqthara.runtime.UsedClasses`. Writing it inside `if true` keeps the
# registration conditional, so this probe fails if the backend ever hoists it to
# compile time or drops it. `xs.get` is an ordinary virtual call on a Java
# receiver, which is C10.3.
use java.lang.Math
use java.lang.String
use java.util.ArrayList
print Math.max(7, 2)
print String.valueOf(42)
xs = ArrayList()
xs.add("b")
xs.add("a")
print xs.get(0)
if true
  use java.time.LocalDate
  print LocalDate(2026, 1, 1).toString()
end
